{%- liquid
  assign _seo_noindex = false
  assign _seo_noindex_follow = false
  if request.page_type == 'cart' or request.page_type == 'search'
    assign _seo_noindex = true
  elsif request.page_type contains 'customers/'
    assign _seo_noindex = true
  elsif template.name == 'collection'
    if current_tags
      assign _seo_noindex = true
    else
      assign _noindex_handles = 'reseller-only,redesign-test-collection,menu-booths-redesign,menu-booths,accessories-test-only,all-for-reseller,globofilter-best-selling-products-index' | split: ','
      if _noindex_handles contains collection.handle
        assign _seo_noindex = true
      endif
    endif
  elsif template.name == 'blog' and current_tags
    assign _seo_noindex_follow = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if _seo_noindex -%}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
{%- elsif _seo_noindex_follow -%}
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  This snippet now ONLY handles the noindex robots meta above
  (cart / search / customer / filtered-collection / internal-collection pages).

  The en-GB hreflang injection that used to live here was REMOVED (2026-05).
  It emitted hreflang="en-GB" pointing at the current localised URL on every
  secondary-market page (e.g. /de-de/... claimed to be both de-DE AND en-GB),
  colliding two languages onto one URL and breaking hreflang reciprocity across
  ~10,000 pages (Ahrefs health 2/100, ticket SBS-115).

  Shopify Markets already emits a complete, reciprocal alternate cluster
  natively (en + x-default -> the UK primary URL), so an explicit en-GB tag is
  unnecessary and was actively harmful. Filename retained to avoid touching the
  8 layout files that render this snippet; rename to seo-noindex.liquid is a
  safe follow-up.
{%- endcomment -%}
